      "tags": ["pangaea", "supercontinent"]
    },
    {
      "ageMa": 252,
      "title": "Permian-Triassic crisis",
      "body": "Massive volcanism and climate stress coincide with Earth's largest known extinction. Tectonics shapes the world that recovers afterward.",
      "camera": [55, 55],
      "tags": ["extinction", "volcanism"]
    },
    {
      "ageMa": 200,
      "title": "Pangaea begins to split",
      "body": "Rifting opens new ocean basins. The first recognizable outlines of the Atlantic story appear.",
      "camera": [-25, 5],
      "tags": ["rift", "atlantic"]
    },
    {
      "ageMa": 150,
      "title": "Atlantic opening accelerates",
      "body": "North America, Africa, and Eurasia separate. Marine gateways and young ocean crust redraw the planet.",
      "camera": [-35, 15],
      "tags": ["atlantic", "jurassic"]
    },
    {
      "ageMa": 100,
      "title": "India races north",
      "body": "India detaches from Gondwana and moves rapidly toward Asia, setting up one of the great mountain-building collisions.",
      "camera": [75, -25],
      "tags": ["india", "gondwana"]
    },
    {
      "ageMa": 66,
      "title": "End-Cretaceous transition",
      "body": "Tectonic provinces are close to familiar positions. Volcanism, changing seas, and impact aftermath reset ecosystems.",
      "camera": [80, 18],
      "tags": ["cretaceous", "transition"]
    },
    {
      "ageMa": 55,
      "title": "Himalaya begins rising",
      "body": "India collides with Eurasia. Crust thickens, the Himalaya and Tibetan Plateau rise, and monsoons eventually reorganize.",
      "camera": [82, 30],
      "tags": ["himalaya", "collision"]
    },
    {
      "ageMa": 34,
      "title": "Antarctica isolates",
      "body": "Southern Ocean circulation strengthens as Antarctica becomes more isolated, encouraging long-term glaciation.",
